1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:02,008
(Q1（form）) Good morning. How can I help you?

2
00:00:02,008 --> 00:00:05,771
Hello. I'm interested in renting a house somewhere in the town.

3
00:00:05,771 --> 00:00:09,142
Right. Could I have your name please?

4
00:00:09,142 --> 00:00:11,205
Yes, it's Steven Godfrey.

5
00:00:11,205 --> 00:00:14,922
And tell me how many bedrooms you're looking for.

6
00:00:14,922 --> 00:00:20,005
Well, we'd need four, because I'm going to share the house with three friends.

7
00:00:20,005 --> 00:00:23,706
Okay, there are several of that size on our books.

8
00:00:23,706 --> 00:00:27,288
They mostly belong to families who are working abroad at the moment.

9
00:00:27,288 --> 00:00:36,072
[Q1答案句] What about the location?：It'd be nice to be central.：That might be difficult, as most houses of that size are in the suburbs.

10
00:00:36,072 --> 00:00:40,734
(Q2) Still, there are a few. What's your upper limit for the rent?

11
00:00:40,734 --> 00:00:50,329
[Q2答案句： up to=maximum] We'd like something around ￡500 a month, but we could go up to ￡600 if we have to. But we can't go beyond that.

12
00:00:50,329 --> 00:00:56,458
(Q3) Do you know how long you want to rent the house for? The minimum let is six months, as you probably realise.

13
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,000
⭐

14
00:00:56,458 --> 00:01:02,699
[Q3答案句： 对方问（定位词） + 另一人回答（答案句）] We're at college here for two years, and we don't want to have to move during that time if we can avoid it.

15
00:01:02,699 --> 00:01:08,579
Right. And how soon do you want to move in? All our lets start on the first of the month.

16
00:01:08,579 --> 00:01:13,046
Well, as soon as possible, really, so that means September 1st.

17
00:01:13,046 --> 00:01:21,276
(Q4（table）) Okay, let me have a look at what we've got We have photographs of all the houses on our books, so you can get an idea of what they're like.

18
00:01:21,276 --> 00:01:34,089
[Q4答案句： doesn't have = no] There's this one in Oakington Avenue, at 550 pounds a month. Combined living room and dining room, with a separate kitchen.&nbsp;It doesn't have a garage, though you can park in the road.

19
00:01:34,089 --> 00:01:37,189
Ah, we'd prefer to have one, if possible.

20
00:01:37,189 --> 00:01:41,622
(Q5) Right. Then have a look at this house, in Mead Street.

21
00:01:41,622 --> 00:01:46,030
It's got a very large living room and kitchen, bathroom, cloakroom...

22
00:01:46,030 --> 00:01:47,014
How much is it?

23
00:01:47,014 --> 00:01:51,766
That one's 580. It's very well furnished and equipped.

24
00:01:51,766 --> 00:02:04,338
[Q5答案句， 一个人说 big=large，跟出答案词， 另一人态度是 觉得不OK， 符合表头「problem」] It also has plenty of space for parking, and it's available for a minimum of a year. Oh, and there's a big garden.I don't think we could cope with that, to be honest. We'll be too busy to look after it.

25
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,000
⭐

26
00:02:04,338 --> 00:02:14,241
(Q6) [Q6答案句] Okay. Then there's this older house in Hamilton Road: living room, kitchen-diner, and it has a study. 550 a month.

27
00:02:14,241 --> 00:02:23,478
(Q7) [Q7答案句： 听adj, 属于「问题」方面的] That looks rather nice. But whereabouts in Hamilton Road? ： Towards the western end.：Oh, that'll be very noisy. I know the area.

28
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,000


29
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,000


30
00:02:23,478 --> 00:02:27,515
Yes, it's pretty lively. Some people like it, though.&nbsp;

31
00:02:27,515 --> 00:02:33,276
(Q8) Well, what about this house in Devon Close?Devon Close，That looks lovely.

32
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,000


33
00:02:33,276 --> 00:02:37,400
There's a big demand for houses in that area, so prices tend to be quite high.

34
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:41,879
But this one hasn't been decorated for a few years, which has kept the rent down a bit.

35
00:02:41,879 --> 00:02:51,267
[Q8答案句：听数字即可] It's got a living room, dining room and small kitchen, and it's 595 a month. I think it would suit you, from what you've said.

36
00:02:51,267 --> 00:02:52,801
It sounds fine.

37
00:02:52,801 --> 00:02:55,888
(Q9&10（多选）) Why's that part of town so popular?

38
00:02:55,888 --> 00:03:01,090
Well, there's a big scheme to improve the district, and it'll soon have the best facilities for miles around.

39
00:03:01,090 --> 00:03:02,423
What sort of thing?

40
00:03:02,423 --> 00:03:07,023
There's a big sports centre under construction, which will be very impressive when it's finished.

41
00:03:07,023 --> 00:03:12,569
In fact the swimming pool's already opened, ahead of schedule, and it's attracting a lot of people.

42
00:03:12,569 --> 00:03:15,618
What about cinemas: are there any in the area?

43
00:03:15,618 --> 00:03:21,460
The only one closed down last year, and it's now in the process of being converted into a film museum.

44
00:03:21,460 --> 00:03:25,228
The local people are trying to get a new cinema added to the scheme.

45
00:03:25,228 --> 00:03:30,983
I think I heard something about a plan to replace the existing concert hall with a larger one.

46
00:03:30,983 --> 00:03:33,860
Ah, that's due to start next year.

47
00:03:33,860 --> 00:03:38,457
Well it sounds an interesting area to live in. Could I go and see the house, please?

48
00:03:38,457 --> 00:03:40,957
Yes, of course.

